    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="26">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:VIAtr">VI Atr</ref> 26</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="26" corresp="#wit-k"><pb n="254" ed="#liebermann"/>K. ⁊ sy ælc wydewe, þe hy sylfe mid rihte gehealde, on Godes griðe ⁊ on þæs cynges.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="26" corresp="#wit-d-incomplete"><pb n="254" ed="#liebermann"/>And sy ælc wuduwe, þe hy silfe mid rihte gehealde, on Godes griðe ⁊ on ðæs cynges.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="26" corresp="#wit-k"><pb n="98" ed="#robertson"/>⁊ sy ælc wydewe, þe hy sylfe mid rihte gehealde, on Godes griðe ⁊ on þæs cynges.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-k"><pb n="170" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And sy ælc wydewe, þe hy sylfe mid rihte gehealde on Godes griðe and on þæs cynges.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="255" ed="#liebermann"/>Und<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#VIAtr_26.lnote.de.1"/> jede Wittwe, die sich ehrlich hält, stehe unter Friedensschutz der Kirche und des Königs.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And let every widow who conducts herself rightly be under the protection of God and of the king.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-k"><ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#missing"/><pb n="99" ed="#robertson"/>And all widows who lead a respectable life shall enjoy the special protection of God and of the king.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-k"><pb n="171" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And all widows who comport themselves properly shall be under the protection of God and the king.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="255"><ref target="clause:VAtr_21">V Atr 21</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">ebd. 21</note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="340"><label>parallel (VI version)</label> <ref target="clause:VAtr_21">V Atr 21</ref> <quote>n. 352: V Atr 21 (VI 26)</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-ppmel" n="70"><label>parallel</label> <ref target="clause:VAtr_21">V Atr 21–21.1</ref> <quote>V Atr 21 – 21:1 (VI 26 – 26:1)</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#kennedy" n="59"><label>source in V–VIII Æthelred</label> <ref target="clause:Cn-1018_part-049">Cn 1018 16–16.1</ref> <quote>Kennedy’s table: VI Æthelred 26, VI Æthelred 26.1 | D 16–16.1 | II Cnut 73</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#kennedy" n="60"><label>appear again as</label> <ref target="clause:IICn_73">II Cn 73</ref> <quote>VI Atr. 26 and 26.1, which appear again as II Cn. 73.</quote></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="VIAtr_26.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">176</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">benutzt durch <hi rend="italic">Hom. n</hi>. Wulfstan 271</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">used by <hi rend="italic">Hom. n</hi>. Wulfstan 271</seg><note type="remark" resp="#claude">On several rubrics: VI Atr 26. 26, 1</note></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="VIAtr_26.lnote.de.a" n="a" source="#liebermann-erkl" rend="wholeClause"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">176</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Wie <hi rend="italic">o</hi>. 13. <hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Frieden 5a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">As <hi rend="italic">above</hi> 13. <hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Frieden 5a</seg></note>
      </div>
